# Mobile app environment template.
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (gitignored) for local development:
#   Windows:  copy .env.example .env.local
#   macOS/*nix: cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Expo's CLI loads `.env.local` automatically at startup, and app.config.ts
# resolves the API base URL the app talks to. Resolution order (first wins):
#
#   1. .env.<APP_ENV>     — loaded when APP_ENV is set. `npm run dev:mobile:cloud`
#                           sets APP_ENV=dev, loading `.env.dev` to run a DEV
#                           build against the HOSTED (Render) API. Falls back to
#                           the Render default if `.env.dev` is absent.
#   2. API_BASE_URL       — explicit override for ANY other context.
#   3. PROD_API_BASE_URL  — used only for release builds/exports
#                           (NODE_ENV=production). Defaults to the Render URL.
#   4. built-in default   — the Android emulator route, for local `expo start`.
#
# So a normal `npm run dev:mobile` hits your local API automatically, a
# production build (expo export / EAS) targets the hosted API automatically,
# and `npm run dev:mobile:cloud` runs a dev build against the hosted API.
# You only need to set anything below if you want to override those defaults.

# Local dev target — OPTIONAL. Leave commented to use the built-in default
# (http://10.0.2.2:3000, the Android emulator route). Uncomment and edit ONLY
# if your local target differs. Note: API_BASE_URL wins in every context, so
# if you uncomment it here it also applies to local production exports — that's
# fine for EAS/CI builds (no .env.local there), just be aware on your machine.
#   iOS simulator:     http://localhost:3000
#   Physical phone:    http://<your-LAN-IP>:3000  (e.g. http://192.168.1.50:3000)
# API_BASE_URL=http://10.0.2.2:3000

# Hosted API used by release builds. Only needed if your Render URL differs
# from the default in app.config.ts.
# PROD_API_BASE_URL=https://dwt-api.onrender.com

# Hosted "dev" target — run a DEV build against the hosted (Render) backend
# with `npm run dev:mobile:cloud` (sets APP_ENV=dev, which loads `.env.dev`).
# OPTIONAL: the cloud script already defaults to the Render URL, so you only
# need `.env.dev` if you want to point it somewhere else. To create it:
#   Windows:    copy .env.example .env.dev
#   macOS/*nix: cp .env.example .env.dev
# then set API_BASE_URL in `.env.dev` to your hosted URL, e.g.:
# API_BASE_URL=https://dwt-api.onrender.com
